# Family Roots domain & layout test scenarios

Use this as a checklist when adding or changing family-graph, layout, or tree behavior.

## Graph & relationships

- Single person (disconnected)
- Couple + children (two-parent union)
- Single parent + child (`union:single:parentId`)
- Remarriage: child linked to one parent of a couple only
- Child with extra bogus third parent
- Sibling via shared parents vs via marriage only
- Spouse edges vs parent-child direction (parent A → child B)

## Collapse / branch fold

- Fold couple hides descendants + in-laws, keeps parents visible
- Fold one union does not hide sibling partnership children
- Toggle collapse on/off
- `unionsHidingPerson` lists active folds
- Child of other marriage of one parent stays visible when folding unrelated union

## Direct line & search

- Direct line includes ancestors + descendants, excludes siblings and spouses
- Union highlighting on blood line only
- Search: empty query, case insensitivity, maiden name, birth place, no matches, limit

## Commands & audit

- `planAddRelative`: child, parent, spouse, sibling; missing anchor; sibling without parents
- `auditFamily`: disconnected, unknown gender, uncertain links, clean tree

## Layout invariants (see `layout-invariants.test.ts`)

| Scenario | Intent |
|----------|--------|
| Couple + two children | Spouses adjacent, children below |
| Wide vs narrow cousins | No false widening between branches |
| One child per branch | Compact parent spacing |
| Equal cousin fans | Symmetric gaps |
| Widest generation | Fan wider than youngest tail |
| Cross-family marriage | Couple between natal sibling runs |
| Only-child marriage | Packs beside in-law siblings |
| Remove marriage | Person returns to natal sibling row |
| Two spouses | Separate child sets under each union |
| Collapsed union | Stays between visible parents |
| Disconnected components | No mutual overlap |

## Display vs structure (performance)

- Draft rename → `applyDisplayPatches` updates labels, not x/y
- `layoutModelStructureKey` unchanged on rename, changed on birth year
- `computeTreeLayoutAsync` completes; worker failure falls back to main thread

## Dates

- `16.07.1956`, `1956`, month precision via `parsePartialDateInput`
- Living vs deceased life span strings

## Commands (see `commands.test.ts`)

| Kind | Expect |
|------|--------|
| child | parent_child edge anchor → new |
| parent | parent_child edge new → anchor |
| spouse | spouse edge |
| sibling | one parent_child per known parent |
| missing anchor | error |
| sibling w/o parents | error |

## Layout structure key (see `apply-display-patches.test.ts`)

- Unchanged: rename, maiden name, death year, notes
- Changed: birth year, new relationship, collapse toggle

## Worker / async layout (see `compute-layout-async.test.ts`)

- Main-thread success for small tree
- Worker timeout → main-thread fallback (fake timers)
- postMessage throw → main-thread fallback

## Performance guards (`layout-performance.test.ts`)

- Aguilar interactive layout &lt; 20s
- Structure key stable across rename-only edits
